// Logical Model for the Permission Ticket (Portable Kernel Redesign)
// NOTE: This FSH logical model is a best-effort structural overview.
// The authoritative source for field requirements, conditional cardinality,
// and cross-field invariants is the specification prose and TypeScript model.
// FSH cannot express conditional constraints like "resource_type is required
// when kind=data"; those are documented textually in element descriptions.
Logical: PermissionTicket
Title: "Permission Ticket (JWT Payload)"
Description: "Portable kernel of a Permission Ticket. Includes the JWT security envelope, subject identification, optional requester, access grant semantics, workflow context, unified presenter binding, and optional must-understand extensibility."
* iss 1..1 string "Issuer URL"
* aud 1..* uri "Audience (recipient URL(s) or trust framework identifier)"
* exp 1..1 integer "Expiration Timestamp"
* iat 0..1 integer "Issued-At Timestamp"
* jti 1..1 string "Unique Ticket ID"
* ticket_type 1..1 uri "Ticket type URI identifying the ticket schema and processing rules"
* presenter_binding 0..1 BackboneElement "Unified presenter binding container. key and framework_client are independent; either may appear alone, or both may appear together."
  * key 0..1 BackboneElement "Exact-key binding (replaces RFC 7800 cnf; identical semantics)"
    * jkt 1..1 string "JWK Thumbprint (RFC 7638) of the authorized client key"
  * framework_client 0..1 BackboneElement "Trust-framework client identity binding"
    * framework 1..1 uri "Framework instance URI"
    * framework_type 1..1 code "Framework family: well-known | udap"
    * entity_uri 1..1 uri "Framework-recognized client entity URI"
* revocation 0..1 BackboneElement "Revocation Information"
  * url 1..1 url "URL of the Credential Revocation List (CRL)"
  * rid 1..1 string "Revocation Identifier (opaque, max 24 chars)"
* must_understand 0..* string "Payload claim names the recipient MUST understand beyond the base kernel. Inspired by JWS crit (RFC 7515), applied to payload claims."
* subject 1..1 BackboneElement "Subject whose data may be accessed"
  * patient 1..1 Patient "Inline patient facts for recipient-side resolution. May be thin."
  * recipient_record 0..1 Reference "Optional recipient-local patient locator"
* requester 0..1 Resource "Issuer-attested real-world party for whom the grant exists. Typical types: RelatedPerson, Practitioner, PractitionerRole, Organization."
* access 1..1 BackboneElement "Normative authorization model"
  * permissions 1..* BackboneElement "One or more permission rules. When kind=data: resource_type and interactions are required (interactions must be non-empty). When kind=operation: name is required."
    * kind 1..1 code "Permission kind: data | operation"
    * resource_type 0..1 string "FHIR resource type (or * for broad access). Required when kind=data."
    * interactions 0..* code "REST interactions: read | search | history | create | update | patch | delete. Required and non-empty when kind=data."
    * category_any_of 0..* Coding "Category filter group (OR within group). Only when kind=data."
    * code_any_of 0..* Coding "Code filter group (OR within group). Only when kind=data."
    * name 0..1 string "Operation name when kind=operation. Required when kind=operation."
    * target 0..1 Reference "Operation target. Only when kind=operation."
  * data_period 0..1 Period "One coarse timeframe. Mint separate tickets for disjoint windows."
  * jurisdictions 0..* Address "Coarse geographic restriction (country/state only)"
  * source_organizations 0..* Identifier "Positive data-holder scoping by organizational identity"
  * sensitive_data 0..1 code "exclude | include. If absent, recipients default to exclude."
* context 1..1 BackboneElement "Ticket-type-specific mandatory workflow semantics"
  * kind 1..1 code "Context family: patient-access | public-health | social-care-referral | payer-claims | research | provider-consult"
  * reportable_condition 0..1 CodeableConcept "Public health: reportable condition"
  * investigation_case 0..1 Identifier "Public health: case identifier"
  * triggering_resource 0..1 Resource "Public health: triggering Condition, Observation, or DiagnosticReport"
  * source_report 0..1 Resource "Public health: source DocumentReference"
  * concern 0..1 CodeableConcept "Social care: concern being addressed"
  * referral 0..1 Resource "Social care: referral ServiceRequest"
  * task 0..1 Resource "Social care: supporting Task"
  * service 0..1 CodeableConcept "Payer claims: service being adjudicated"
  * claim 0..1 Resource "Payer claims: Claim artifact"
  * study 0..1 Resource "Research: ResearchStudy artifact"
  * research_subject 0..1 Resource "Research: ResearchSubject artifact"
  * condition 0..1 CodeableConcept "Research: condition of interest"
  * reason 0..1 CodeableConcept "Provider consult: reason for consult"
  * consult_request 0..1 Resource "Provider consult: ServiceRequest"
* supporting_artifacts 0..* Resource "Optional evidence and review material. Not required for the base protocol's yes/no decision."
